# Codex model + reasoning-effort tiers for CI agent roles.
#
# Single source of truth: bump a model id or effort level here and every
# role that references that tier picks it up on the next run. Which tier
# a given role uses is decided where that role is wired up (e.g. the role
# case statement in review-reviewer.yml, or the workflow that invokes
# .devcontainer/configure-codex.sh directly), not here — this file only
# answers "what does 'frontier' / 'luna' currently mean".
#
# Policy (docs/agentic-pipeline-learnings.md §2.12): judgment-heavy roles
# (fixer, issue author, design review, security review) use FRONTIER.
# Mechanical/pattern-matching roles (docs consistency, prompt parity,
# test-coverage enforcement, smoke tests, workflow-failure diagnosis) use
# LUNA. CODEX_MODEL_FRONTIER matches CODEX_MODEL_DEFAULT in
# .devcontainer/configure-codex.sh, so a caller that never sources this
# file (or omits CODEX_MODEL) still lands on the frontier model.
CODEX_MODEL_FRONTIER=gpt-5.6-sol
CODEX_REASONING_FRONTIER=high

CODEX_MODEL_LUNA=gpt-5.6-luna
CODEX_REASONING_LUNA=low
